cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: 'One Gap, Three Answers: A Calculus Analysis of Receptive and Expressive Language Development'
type: software
authors:
- family-names: Rollo
  given-names: Nicole
abstract: Reproducible calculus analysis of group-level receptive- and expressive-language trajectories
  in Down syndrome and Fragile X syndrome. The project compares an absolute score gap, a proportional
  gap, and a chronological time gap, and uses the Mean Value Theorem to connect score separation
  with time separation.
keywords:
- calculus
- mathematical modeling
- developmental trajectories
- receptive language
- expressive language
- Down syndrome
- Fragile X syndrome
- reproducibility
